1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:01,910
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:03,680
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,140
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:07,950
(Episode 54)

5
00:00:21,430 --> 00:00:22,430
Where did she go?

6
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:26,600
Seok Jin!

7
00:00:52,790 --> 00:00:53,930
Just wait a moment.

8
00:00:53,930 --> 00:00:55,460
I'll have breakfast ready
in no time.

9
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:57,560
Mom?

10
00:00:58,630 --> 00:01:00,800
I made doenjang stew, your favorite.

11
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,970
Take off your jacket first
so the smell doesn't stick to it.

12
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:09,440
Here.

13
00:01:10,780 --> 00:01:13,810
Eat up.
You need a hearty meal before work.

14
00:01:14,510 --> 00:01:15,510
Okay.

15
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:18,820
Try it.

16
00:01:22,950 --> 00:01:24,120
- Is it good?
- Yes.

17
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:33,570
Hey, Hae Ra.

18
00:01:36,470 --> 00:01:37,470
Come have a seat.

19
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:40,040
Seok Jin said
he's taking a day off today.

20
00:01:41,270 --> 00:01:42,270
A day off?

21
00:01:42,470 --> 00:01:44,240
He's taking his mom to the doctor.

22
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:48,010
Didn't she just get a checkup
a little while ago?

23
00:01:48,610 --> 00:01:49,610
Is she not feeling well?

24
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:51,780
No, she didn't seem sick.

25
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:53,520
It's just to check something,
apparently.

26
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:54,950
Check something?

27
00:01:55,950 --> 00:01:57,920
Is that all he said?

28
00:01:58,320 --> 00:01:59,320
Yes.

29
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:01,390
Well, it's always better to go
to the doctor regularly...

30
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:02,890
than to avoid it.

31
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:20,880
Mom, are you good to go?

32
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:26,420
Mr. Seok Jin.

33
00:02:27,850 --> 00:02:30,050
I feel a bit strange.

34
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:33,120
I don't like these clothes.

35
00:02:33,530 --> 00:02:35,260
My hair looks weird too.

36
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:40,970
I want to change
into something else...

37
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:42,870
and redo my hair.

38
00:02:43,370 --> 00:02:44,370
Mom...

39
00:02:46,670 --> 00:02:48,070
Weren't you back to normal?

40
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:51,140
Who's back?

41
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:54,380
Did my honey come back?

42
00:02:57,280 --> 00:02:59,750
Quit messing around, Mom. Mom...

43
00:03:01,390 --> 00:03:02,490
Mom...

44
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:04,360
Mom...

45
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:08,760
What's wrong, Mr. Seok Jin?

46
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:12,030
When psychological
defense mechanisms...

47
00:03:12,030 --> 00:03:14,330
face a strong
external shock or stimulus,

48
00:03:14,670 --> 00:03:18,000
closed-off memory circuits
can momentarily open up.

49
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:21,670
Outwardly, she might seem
like her former adult self,

50
00:03:22,170 --> 00:03:25,140
but it can't be considered
an improvement or a cure.

51
00:03:26,810 --> 00:03:29,350
So you mean she hasn't recovered?

52
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:30,680
That's right.

53
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:33,990
This reaction is closer to
a brief state of neural activation.

54
00:03:35,990 --> 00:03:38,020
Could something like this
happen again?

55
00:03:38,990 --> 00:03:40,490
Whenever she experiences
extreme anxiety,

56
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:42,760
it could happen repeatedly
at any time.

57
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:47,000
Has the patient recently been exposed
to any severe stress?

58
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:49,930
Or suffered an unbearable
psychological shock?

59
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:51,740
No.

60
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:54,010
Not that I'm aware of...

61
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:57,040
No. Absolutely not.

62
00:03:58,540 --> 00:03:59,610
Mom.

63
00:03:59,610 --> 00:04:02,750
If you marry Hae Ra,

64
00:04:04,050 --> 00:04:05,720
my husband will be sad.

65
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:21,270
Mom,

66
00:04:22,330 --> 00:04:23,700
has anything been
troubling you lately?

67
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:27,670
No, nothing.

68
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,040
Are you sure?

69
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:35,350
I told you.
You can tell your son anything.

70
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:41,250
There's nothing.

71
00:04:42,450 --> 00:04:45,890
As long as you're happy,
Mr. Seok Jin,

72
00:04:46,490 --> 00:04:48,030
I'm fine with anything.

73
00:04:54,870 --> 00:04:57,970
All right, let's skip daycare today.

74
00:04:58,500 --> 00:04:59,870
I won't go to work today either.

75
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:02,070
Is that okay?

76
00:05:02,670 --> 00:05:03,680
Yes.

77
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:05,680
Well, then,

78
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:08,550
why don't we head
to the supermarket later?

79
00:05:08,910 --> 00:05:09,910
Sounds good.

80
00:05:10,350 --> 00:05:12,650
Take a nap for now
since you took your medicine.

81
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:15,620
- Okay.
- We'll go this afternoon.

82
00:05:15,950 --> 00:05:17,020
All right.

83
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:35,740
Wait.

84
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:37,440
Where did you get this?

85
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:40,240
- Give that back.
- Hold on.

86
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,650
Are you saying you're going here?

87
00:05:43,750 --> 00:05:44,820
Someone like you?

88
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:45,920
Give it back.

89
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:48,920
Ko Eun Seol,

90
00:05:48,990 --> 00:05:51,820
do you really think you're my rival?

91
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:53,260
Given your caliber?

92
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:59,600
Hovering around Seok Jin
didn't work out,

93
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:01,530
so now you're copying
where I went to school?

94
00:06:01,630 --> 00:06:02,630
Hey,

95
00:06:02,670 --> 00:06:04,200
do you have any idea
how hard it was to get in?

96
00:06:04,370 --> 00:06:07,170
Do you think just dabbling in design
gets you in here?

97
00:06:07,170 --> 00:06:10,710
Knowing it's where you went
to school made me hesitate,

98
00:06:11,010 --> 00:06:12,840
but I'm keeping an open mind
about it.

99
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:17,980
Do you know what tuition costs here?

100
00:06:18,050 --> 00:06:19,680
We're talking tens of thousands
of dollars per semester.

101
00:06:19,750 --> 00:06:20,920
Can you even afford that?

102
00:06:21,990 --> 00:06:22,990
Wait.

103
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:26,220
Did you land yourself
a wealthy sponsor?

104
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:28,760
Yes,

105
00:06:29,230 --> 00:06:30,430
I've got a backer.

106
00:06:30,730 --> 00:06:31,730
What?

107
00:06:32,130 --> 00:06:33,830
So I'm allowed to dream big, right?

108
00:06:44,710 --> 00:06:46,810
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

109
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:01,190
Right, thanks.

110
00:07:02,930 --> 00:07:05,260
While it isn't common,

111
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:07,470
we do encounter patients like this.

112
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:12,440
Then is this a sign
that her condition is improving?

113
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:13,640
Yes.

114
00:07:13,970 --> 00:07:15,770
You could see it that way, but...

115
00:07:17,180 --> 00:07:19,310
After enduring
a severe emotional shock,

116
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:22,250
the brain is repeatedly exposed
to specific stimuli.

117
00:07:22,450 --> 00:07:24,520
Through this exposure,
patients sometimes...

118
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:26,350
gradually recover
their sense of reality.

119
00:07:28,250 --> 00:07:29,320
Really?

120
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:34,690
What if she ends up remembering
what happened that day?

121
00:07:55,510 --> 00:07:58,080
Still, it brings relief to see
your mother looking peaceful.

122
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:00,990
This must be hard on you.

123
00:08:03,390 --> 00:08:05,860
So, you want to know
what happened that day?

124
00:08:06,890 --> 00:08:09,260
- Yes.
- The day your father died,

125
00:08:09,690 --> 00:08:11,430
your mother was in shock,

126
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:13,730
but she still handled
all the arrangements well.

127
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:18,700
But a month or so
after the accident,

128
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:21,870
she said she had to go meet someone
to confirm something.

129
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:25,210
She called to ask me to watch you,

130
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:28,680
and her voice was shaking so much.

131
00:08:30,450 --> 00:08:33,180
I offered to go with her,
but she refused,

132
00:08:33,450 --> 00:08:34,720
saying she'd go alone.

133
00:08:36,390 --> 00:08:37,860
Once she got back home,

134
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:40,120
she didn't leave her room for days.

135
00:08:40,490 --> 00:08:42,860
Then she collapsed,
and when she woke up,

136
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:45,900
she had the mind of a child.

137
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:52,870
So...

138
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:56,470
after meeting that person
to verify something...

139
00:08:56,470 --> 00:08:57,610
That's right.

140
00:08:58,310 --> 00:09:01,110
No matter how hard we pressed,
she couldn't remember that day.

141
00:09:01,610 --> 00:09:03,610
If only she'd left us a hint,
we could look into it.

142
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:10,120
To this day, we still have no idea
what happened.

143
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:15,930
I'll have to find out who she met
and what they talked about.

144
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:17,860
Seok Jin.

145
00:09:22,430 --> 00:09:23,870
Don't push yourself too hard.

146
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:26,400
It's already been over 20 years.

147
00:09:27,370 --> 00:09:30,940
We traced her whereabouts back then,

148
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:33,180
but it was no use.

149
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:36,410
It's a miracle
she's doing this well.

150
00:09:37,780 --> 00:09:40,750
So put it behind you,
and just live in peace.

151
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:48,660
Right.

152
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:52,430
Come in, Director Joo.

153
00:09:54,070 --> 00:09:56,270
Were you able to meet
So Yeon's doctor?

154
00:09:57,640 --> 00:10:00,370
Yes, and he went over everything
in detail.

155
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:04,210
Nothing serious happened, right?

156
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:08,250
Apparently, So Yeon had...

157
00:10:08,310 --> 00:10:10,580
a brief moment of clarity
this morning.

158
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:12,550
This morning?

159
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:14,890
Her doctor assured me
it's only temporary...

160
00:10:15,090 --> 00:10:16,320
and fairly common,

161
00:10:16,750 --> 00:10:18,460
so don't worry too much,
Director Joo.

162
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:20,960
He said it doesn't pose
any health risk.

163
00:10:21,460 --> 00:10:23,390
I see. That's a relief.

164
00:10:24,030 --> 00:10:26,100
How are the preparations
for Hae Ra's engagement going?

165
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,870
Pretty good. Here.

166
00:10:28,170 --> 00:10:29,600
This is the guest list.

167
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:31,370
Right, thank you.

168
00:10:33,170 --> 00:10:34,910
Let's see.

169
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:41,580
Dad.

170
00:10:42,150 --> 00:10:44,920
Wait. Still awake, sweetheart?

171
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:47,150
I was waiting for you.

172
00:10:48,450 --> 00:10:50,250
Of course. My daughter's the best.

173
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:53,820
Eun Seol.

174
00:10:55,990 --> 00:10:56,990
Here.

175
00:10:57,860 --> 00:11:01,030
At my last driving job,
they were selling these.

176
00:11:01,470 --> 00:11:02,500
So...

177
00:11:02,970 --> 00:11:05,640
I bought some
because it reminded me of your mom.

178
00:11:05,970 --> 00:11:07,910
She loved hotteok so much.

179
00:11:08,740 --> 00:11:10,780
Yes, she did.

180
00:11:10,780 --> 00:11:12,040
It wasn't just her.

181
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:13,440
You loved them too.

182
00:11:14,050 --> 00:11:16,950
You take right after her,
even your taste in food.

183
00:11:21,090 --> 00:11:23,550
All right. Here you go.

184
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:26,190
Chew it well before you swallow.

185
00:11:27,930 --> 00:11:28,930
Thanks.

186
00:11:31,030 --> 00:11:33,260
Don't share it with the others.
Eat it all yourself.

187
00:11:34,270 --> 00:11:36,130
- I'll put the rest in the fridge.
- Dad.

188
00:11:40,170 --> 00:11:41,370
There's something I want to ask.

189
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:43,940
What is it?

190
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:47,610
By any chance,

191
00:11:48,610 --> 00:11:50,250
when you went to see Director Joo,

192
00:11:51,650 --> 00:11:52,820
did you bring up money?

193
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:55,790
Money?

194
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:01,130
Who do you think?
She's Eun Seol's mom.

195
00:12:02,330 --> 00:12:03,960
- What?
- Half a million dollars.

196
00:12:04,630 --> 00:12:06,260
That's 100,000 dollars times 5.

197
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:08,430
Could it be that 500,000 dollars?

198
00:12:09,470 --> 00:12:10,530
Half a million dollars?

199
00:12:12,140 --> 00:12:14,000
Why did you go to her
without even telling me...

200
00:12:14,070 --> 00:12:15,410
and ask for money?

201
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:18,640
Eun Seol, there seems to be
a misunderstanding.

202
00:12:21,250 --> 00:12:22,610
Did you really have
to demand money...

203
00:12:24,750 --> 00:12:26,680
just for raising me?

204
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:28,550
Ko Eun Seol.

205
00:12:29,350 --> 00:12:30,420
Are you...

206
00:12:30,890 --> 00:12:32,490
seriously doubting me?

207
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:33,560
That's right.

208
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:35,360
I don't get you.

209
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:37,360
Now I really don't.

210
00:12:38,030 --> 00:12:40,530
Was getting that money
really necessary?

211
00:12:41,630 --> 00:12:42,700
No, that's not it.

212
00:13:31,650 --> 00:13:32,980
- Are you from the motel?
- Yes.

213
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:37,050
Gosh, thank you.

214
00:13:42,690 --> 00:13:43,690
(To: An Guk Cheol)

215
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:48,830
(Paternity Test Results)

216
00:13:51,270 --> 00:13:53,100
(A 99.999 percent genetic match)

217
00:13:53,870 --> 00:13:55,110
Yes!

218
00:13:58,810 --> 00:14:00,080
Everything's settled now.

219
00:14:00,610 --> 00:14:01,610
My daughter,

220
00:14:02,450 --> 00:14:04,780
wait for me. Dad's coming for you.

221
00:14:07,950 --> 00:14:09,550
Boss, after work today,

222
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:11,320
I'll pick Teun Teun up
from kindergarten.

223
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:15,060
- Would that really be okay?
- Of course.

224
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:17,630
He doesn't have taekwondo today.

225
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,360
I thought we could drop by
the stationery store.

226
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:26,140
Why are you looking at me like that?

227
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:28,540
Do I have something on my face?

228
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:31,380
Like I said before,

229
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:34,110
people in the neighborhood
are suspicious about us.

230
00:14:34,550 --> 00:14:35,810
Let them be.

231
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:39,420
Besides, it's not even
a suspicion anymore.

232
00:14:41,050 --> 00:14:42,890
I wouldn't have started anything...

233
00:14:42,890 --> 00:14:45,260
if I'd ever doubted my feelings
for you.

234
00:14:48,330 --> 00:14:49,390
So...

235
00:14:50,330 --> 00:14:52,260
If anyone says anything,
I'll just tell them.

236
00:14:52,530 --> 00:14:54,870
We aren't a rumor or a suspicion.
What we have is real.

237
00:15:01,210 --> 00:15:03,870
I mean, if we say it's real,
what can they even say?

238
00:15:04,610 --> 00:15:06,110
If it's the real deal, game over.

239
00:15:09,410 --> 00:15:11,020
I organized the list
of on-site candidates...

240
00:15:11,250 --> 00:15:12,980
by period and recommendation rank.

241
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:15,350
Yes, good work.

242
00:15:15,820 --> 00:15:17,150
You put this together very well.

243
00:15:17,150 --> 00:15:20,020
Right. Is there anything else
you'd like me to do?

244
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:23,690
Secretary Choi, you know I'm getting
engaged this week, right?

245
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:25,760
- You should come, too.
- Why should I?

246
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,770
If your boss tells you to come,
you come.

247
00:15:29,670 --> 00:15:32,940
The rest of my team is coming, too.
Right, Ko Eun Seol?

248
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:34,440
Yes.

249
00:15:36,070 --> 00:15:38,880
Once Ms. Ko and I
narrow down the finalists,

250
00:15:39,210 --> 00:15:41,010
reach out to them, Secretary Choi.

251
00:15:41,110 --> 00:15:42,110
Yes, ma'am.

252
00:15:52,690 --> 00:15:54,590
How is So Yeon doing?

253
00:15:55,730 --> 00:15:57,930
She's been stable
ever since that day.

254
00:15:58,900 --> 00:15:59,960
That's a relief.

255
00:16:00,660 --> 00:16:02,230
How's the engagement planning going?

256
00:16:02,370 --> 00:16:05,770
Yes, Hae Ra and I checked out
the venue yesterday.

257
00:16:05,770 --> 00:16:06,870
Good.

258
00:16:07,100 --> 00:16:08,810
Being so thorough,

259
00:16:08,870 --> 00:16:10,910
she must've handled everything well
in her own style.

260
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:15,880
She hasn't been in your room,
Mr. Seok Jin.

261
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:19,220
Wait. Last time,

262
00:16:19,220 --> 00:16:23,250
Director Joo came in
to check your clothes.

263
00:16:24,090 --> 00:16:25,220
Excuse me, Director.

264
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:28,230
Did you happen to see...

265
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:30,430
a lighter in my room?

266
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:32,400
A lighter?

267
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:34,600
It was definitely in the closet,
but I can't seem to find it.

268
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:37,840
That day,

269
00:16:38,470 --> 00:16:40,840
I briefly went into your room...

270
00:16:40,900 --> 00:16:42,970
to check the size of your suit.

271
00:16:43,370 --> 00:16:45,980
But I didn't see a lighter.

272
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:49,310
Besides, you don't even smoke.

273
00:16:50,410 --> 00:16:51,750
It belonged to my father.

274
00:16:52,620 --> 00:16:54,650
Oh, I see.

275
00:16:56,820 --> 00:17:00,220
Never mind.
I'll look for it again carefully.

276
00:17:01,330 --> 00:17:04,060
All right. Go on, then.

277
00:17:10,370 --> 00:17:12,000
He noticed...

278
00:17:12,170 --> 00:17:14,340
that the lighter was missing
this soon?

279
00:17:16,070 --> 00:17:17,240
Kang Young Hoon...

280
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:20,610
is pretty obsessed
with that lighter too.

281
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:24,150
What's the deal with it?

282
00:17:37,260 --> 00:17:39,200
(Family Event:
Engagement Announcement)

283
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:41,270
(Design Team Leader Kang Hae Ra
and Planning Director Cha Seok Jin)

284
00:17:43,230 --> 00:17:44,230
Hold on.

285
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:48,210
Those two are getting engaged?

286
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,480
(Congratulations.
Where is it being held?)

287
00:17:53,540 --> 00:17:55,180
H Hotel?

288
00:17:55,510 --> 00:17:56,580
Ho...

289
00:17:58,420 --> 00:18:01,220
Got it! Hanyang Hotel.

290
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:05,660
I mean,
it's my daughter's engagement party.

291
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:08,660
A father can't miss that.

292
00:18:15,330 --> 00:18:16,500
Sir.

293
00:18:17,670 --> 00:18:18,800
It's me.

294
00:18:52,540 --> 00:18:54,770
(Cheongma Group's 50th Anniversary:
Announcing a Global Leap Forward)

295
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:57,110
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation
PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

296
00:18:57,170 --> 00:18:59,240
(Cheongma Design Team Leader
Kang Hae Ra)

297
00:19:13,890 --> 00:19:15,760
An Guk Cheol, darn it.

298
00:19:16,430 --> 00:19:18,760
You piece of garbage.

299
00:19:23,630 --> 00:19:25,140
That woman...

300
00:19:25,670 --> 00:19:28,610
won't lift a single finger.

301
00:19:28,940 --> 00:19:32,710
She left all the dishes
and laundry piling up.

302
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:35,950
Gosh, my whole body aches.

303
00:19:36,810 --> 00:19:37,980
Good grief.

304
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:39,820
Trying to pay back 5,000 dollars...

305
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:42,420
will cost me over 5,000 dollars
in medical bills.

306
00:19:44,190 --> 00:19:46,760
Is there any way
I can come up with that money?

307
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:48,960
Wait.

308
00:19:49,430 --> 00:19:51,660
Maybe I should ask Eun Seol again.

309
00:19:52,230 --> 00:19:56,400
I think I can talk to her quietly,
without her dad finding out.

310
00:19:58,970 --> 00:20:00,600
I'm home.

311
00:20:04,170 --> 00:20:05,510
Grandma?

312
00:20:06,780 --> 00:20:08,850
Are you my boss's new housekeeper?

313
00:20:10,810 --> 00:20:12,920
Hey, Teun Teun, you're back.

314
00:20:19,820 --> 00:20:20,920
What's that?

315
00:20:22,690 --> 00:20:23,960
It's nothing.

316
00:20:24,060 --> 00:20:25,460
Is that so?

317
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:28,130
Anyway...

318
00:20:28,630 --> 00:20:30,500
Did you have something to say?

319
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:32,570
Well, it's nothing big,

320
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:34,910
just about the loan
I mentioned before.

321
00:20:35,140 --> 00:20:36,470
Any chance you can help?

322
00:20:38,140 --> 00:20:39,140
A loan?

323
00:20:39,210 --> 00:20:41,240
If you could pull
a 5,000-dollar employee loan for me,

324
00:20:41,380 --> 00:20:43,380
I'll pay it all back
within three months.

325
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:47,550
What do you need that money for?

326
00:20:47,990 --> 00:20:51,090
I made an investment,
and it didn't pan out.

327
00:20:51,890 --> 00:20:54,830
It's only 5,000 dollars after all,
so do what you can.

328
00:20:55,530 --> 00:20:58,060
You're a designer at a big firm,

329
00:20:58,360 --> 00:21:00,200
so 5,000 dollars should be
a breeze for you.

330
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:04,570
Besides, 5,000 dollars...

331
00:21:05,270 --> 00:21:08,640
doesn't even scratch the surface
of what it cost to raise you.

332
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:11,410
Please get it to me this week.

333
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:23,220
Grandmother, sit down here
for a second.

334
00:21:24,050 --> 00:21:25,060
Why?

335
00:21:32,130 --> 00:21:33,900
So you lost all that money?

336
00:21:35,330 --> 00:21:38,970
If my boss gave you that much money,
you should've told me first.

337
00:21:39,170 --> 00:21:41,510
I already gave her an earful,
so don't be so harsh on her.

338
00:21:42,110 --> 00:21:44,540
Your grandmother and I will
pay it back somehow,

339
00:21:44,610 --> 00:21:45,640
so don't worry.

340
00:21:45,980 --> 00:21:48,880
Teun Teun's mom herself said
she understood.

341
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:49,880
Dad.

342
00:21:50,010 --> 00:21:53,180
Right. If she isn't making a fuss,
why are you?

343
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:54,250
Grandma.

344
00:21:55,190 --> 00:21:57,220
Even if she said that,
we must pay it back immediately.

345
00:21:57,250 --> 00:21:58,660
What are you talking about?

346
00:21:59,590 --> 00:22:01,190
Do none of you have any shame?

347
00:22:08,330 --> 00:22:10,100
Hey, Eun Seol,
come here for a second.

348
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:22,950
You know about
Grandma's mess, right?

349
00:22:23,610 --> 00:22:24,610
Yes.

350
00:22:26,120 --> 00:22:27,580
If you ask me,

351
00:22:28,090 --> 00:22:29,490
we shouldn't put off paying it back.

352
00:22:30,850 --> 00:22:33,560
We'll cover it with
the 50,000-dollar prize you won.

353
00:22:34,660 --> 00:22:35,760
Just take 5,000 dollars out...

354
00:22:35,830 --> 00:22:36,860
Absolutely not.

355
00:22:36,930 --> 00:22:39,060
How could you even think about
touching that money?

356
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:41,600
We'll explain things
to Teun Teun's mom...

357
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:45,500
- and ask for a little more time...
- Fine, pay it back right now.

358
00:22:45,940 --> 00:22:47,700
Besides, that money?

359
00:22:48,140 --> 00:22:49,440
Eun Seol gave it to us
for raising her.

360
00:22:49,510 --> 00:22:51,440
Grandma, do you even hear yourself?

361
00:22:51,610 --> 00:22:54,580
My joints will wear out trying
to scrape together 5,000 dollars.

362
00:22:54,980 --> 00:22:57,380
- Pay it back right now.
- I said no.

363
00:22:58,320 --> 00:23:00,980
- We'll try our best...
- Then what about my boss's money?

364
00:23:01,490 --> 00:23:04,150
- I mean, we have a way to pay her.
- Dad.

365
00:23:06,090 --> 00:23:07,390
I'm moving out.

366
00:23:11,830 --> 00:23:14,000
Whether you take 5,000
from the 50,000 dollars...

367
00:23:14,060 --> 00:23:15,830
or I get a 5,000-dollar loan
for you,

368
00:23:15,830 --> 00:23:16,930
I'll give you the money.

369
00:23:17,770 --> 00:23:18,770
Hey, Ko Eun Seol.

370
00:23:19,970 --> 00:23:21,340
Don't you think
you're crossing the line?

371
00:23:22,070 --> 00:23:23,070
Why?

372
00:23:23,610 --> 00:23:27,180
I just want to live a quiet life.
Can't I even have that?

373
00:23:36,890 --> 00:23:39,460
I'm the one to blame.
It's all my fault.

374
00:23:41,220 --> 00:23:43,160
Was something wrong with So Yeon?

375
00:23:43,560 --> 00:23:45,900
She had a checkup a few days ago.

376
00:23:46,660 --> 00:23:49,230
Chief Cha took her
to get something checked,

377
00:23:49,270 --> 00:23:50,930
but there wasn't anything wrong.

378
00:23:52,070 --> 00:23:53,140
She's not in good health,

379
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:54,970
so she needs to see
a doctor regularly.

380
00:23:55,210 --> 00:23:56,940
Chief Cha must have been busy,

381
00:23:57,240 --> 00:23:59,480
especially with
the engagement coming up.

382
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:01,510
That's why
we need to speed up the wedding,

383
00:24:01,750 --> 00:24:03,380
if only for Chief Cha's sake.

384
00:24:05,950 --> 00:24:08,690
Caring for a sick person
is never easy.

385
00:24:09,220 --> 00:24:12,820
Rather than letting him
shoulder that burden alone,

386
00:24:13,420 --> 00:24:16,660
we can all help out
once they're married.

387
00:24:17,230 --> 00:24:20,760
I had no idea you were
so considerate of Chief Cha.

388
00:24:21,670 --> 00:24:25,700
If we move the wedding up,
Hae Ra will love it.

389
00:24:26,500 --> 00:24:27,900
Once they're married,

390
00:24:27,970 --> 00:24:30,240
tell them to take their time
on their honeymoon.

391
00:24:30,770 --> 00:24:31,980
Under the pretext of being busy,

392
00:24:32,580 --> 00:24:35,250
they haven't been able to go
on proper dates.

393
00:24:36,180 --> 00:24:38,010
They could travel abroad
for a month...

394
00:24:39,220 --> 00:24:41,520
and broaden their view
of the global market.

395
00:24:42,350 --> 00:24:44,550
Yes, that sounds like a great idea.

396
00:24:45,090 --> 00:24:49,190
Right. Then while they are away,
we should take care of So Yeon.

397
00:24:49,890 --> 00:24:52,060
Do you think
Chief Cha would want that?

398
00:24:52,660 --> 00:24:55,130
If we take care of her,
it'll only be a burden to him.

399
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:59,170
We should send So Yeon
with a proper caregiver...

400
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:02,270
to get some fresh air
and relax for a few days.

401
00:25:02,640 --> 00:25:06,610
She has a hard time adjusting
to new environments.

402
00:25:07,510 --> 00:25:08,580
Will she be okay?

403
00:25:08,950 --> 00:25:10,650
We can figure that out later.

404
00:25:11,080 --> 00:25:13,420
Let's focus on preparing
for their wedding first.

405
00:25:14,780 --> 00:25:17,790
I'll check the hotel availability
for the wedding right away.

406
00:25:22,960 --> 00:25:25,330
I have to get them
married off quickly.

407
00:25:26,830 --> 00:25:28,800
When they leave for their honeymoon,

408
00:25:30,130 --> 00:25:32,540
that's when I should strike.

409
00:25:40,180 --> 00:25:41,180
Mr. Seok Jin,

410
00:25:42,380 --> 00:25:44,080
you look so handsome today.

411
00:25:46,150 --> 00:25:47,180
You look pretty too, Mom.

412
00:25:48,250 --> 00:25:51,320
Now, only happiness lies ahead.

413
00:25:54,620 --> 00:25:55,790
That must be true, right?

414
00:25:57,190 --> 00:25:58,190
Mom.

415
00:25:59,260 --> 00:26:00,660
Am I making the right choice?

416
00:26:02,900 --> 00:26:03,900
Yes.

417
00:26:04,500 --> 00:26:07,340
You've always done well,
Mr. Seok Jin.

418
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:11,410
So I'm sure everything else
will turn out great too.

419
00:26:30,490 --> 00:26:31,800
Absolutely gorgeous.

420
00:26:32,500 --> 00:26:33,530
Director Joo,

421
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:36,400
doesn't Hae Ra look stunning today?

422
00:26:37,330 --> 00:26:39,740
Imagine how stunning she'll be
on her wedding day.

423
00:26:40,440 --> 00:26:43,840
Just thinking about it
makes me tear up.

424
00:26:45,440 --> 00:26:47,240
Yes, it really does.

425
00:26:47,580 --> 00:26:50,210
Of course. Not just anyone
can pull off this dress.

426
00:26:58,820 --> 00:26:59,890
Director Joo,

427
00:27:00,590 --> 00:27:01,860
are those tears?

428
00:27:04,030 --> 00:27:07,360
Tears, when this isn't even
the wedding?

429
00:27:07,860 --> 00:27:09,230
She saw wrong, right?

430
00:27:09,330 --> 00:27:11,770
Of course.
I just got something in my eye.

431
00:27:16,310 --> 00:27:17,710
I think it's time.

432
00:27:17,810 --> 00:27:18,910
Let's go, Mom.

433
00:27:26,820 --> 00:27:30,320
Yes, you deserve
only the best in life.

434
00:27:31,490 --> 00:27:34,020
Down to the very last grain of sand
under your feet,

435
00:27:34,760 --> 00:27:36,190
I'll sweep it all away for you.

436
00:27:39,160 --> 00:27:40,160
This is nice.

437
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:42,770
Would I ever get an engagement party
in a place like this?

438
00:27:43,500 --> 00:27:45,040
No, will I even be able
to get married?

439
00:27:45,870 --> 00:27:46,870
You're right.

440
00:27:47,100 --> 00:27:48,740
Even if we do,
it won't be anywhere like this.

441
00:27:49,870 --> 00:27:52,710
Anyway, Chief Cha
has really struck it rich now.

442
00:27:53,140 --> 00:27:56,110
He's about to be the one and
only son-in-law of Cheongma Group.

443
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:58,380
Maybe I should hit on...

444
00:27:59,250 --> 00:28:00,920
the youngest daughter
of some conglomerate.

445
00:28:01,820 --> 00:28:02,820
In your dreams.

446
00:28:04,120 --> 00:28:05,190
What do you mean, in my dreams?

447
00:28:34,950 --> 00:28:36,950
(Kang Hae Ra and Cha Seok Jin)

448
00:28:40,460 --> 00:28:41,690
Kang Hae Ra.

449
00:29:06,420 --> 00:29:10,350
That wraps up the introduction
of our lovely couple.

450
00:29:10,620 --> 00:29:13,020
Next, we will hear...

451
00:29:13,260 --> 00:29:15,890
their engagement vows to each other.

452
00:29:16,260 --> 00:29:17,630
A round of applause, please.

453
00:29:22,500 --> 00:29:23,600
Mr. Seok Jin.

454
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:25,500
- Engagement vows.
- Engagement vows.

455
00:29:26,170 --> 00:29:27,170
- Today, as we take...
- Today, as we take...

456
00:29:27,170 --> 00:29:28,200
- our first step...
- our first step...

457
00:29:28,270 --> 00:29:31,110
- toward a life together,
- toward a life together,

458
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:32,840
- before our families...
- before our families...

459
00:29:32,840 --> 00:29:35,450
- and honored guests,
- Hi!

460
00:29:35,480 --> 00:29:37,550
- we make the following pledge.
- How lovely.

461
00:29:38,680 --> 00:29:40,080
In every moment
of preparing for marriage...

462
00:29:40,180 --> 00:29:42,420
and envisioning our future together,

463
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:45,090
I will listen to my bride,
Kang Hae Ra,

464
00:29:45,590 --> 00:29:48,960
and prepare to be a loving husband
who grows alongside her.

465
00:29:49,830 --> 00:29:51,760
While painting our future together,

466
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:54,560
so the groom, Cha Seok Jin,
never carries the burden alone,

467
00:29:54,860 --> 00:29:56,500
I will always stand closest to him,

468
00:29:56,570 --> 00:29:58,800
and become a partner
who walks beside him.

469
00:29:59,500 --> 00:30:01,440
- Through our engagement,
- Through our engagement,

470
00:30:01,640 --> 00:30:03,440
- we'll love and know each other...
- we'll love and know each other...

471
00:30:03,510 --> 00:30:05,010
- even more deeply.
- even more deeply.

472
00:30:05,340 --> 00:30:07,280
- With joyful hearts...
- With joyful hearts...

473
00:30:07,380 --> 00:30:08,710
- until our wedding day,
- until our wedding day,

474
00:30:08,950 --> 00:30:10,310
- we'll build our future...
- we'll build our future...

475
00:30:10,380 --> 00:30:11,750
- step by step.
- step by step.

476
00:30:12,280 --> 00:30:14,320
- We thank everyone...
- We thank everyone...

477
00:30:14,320 --> 00:30:15,490
- who has blessed us today.
- who has blessed us today.

478
00:30:16,090 --> 00:30:18,490
- November 8, 2026.
- November 8, 2026.

479
00:30:18,890 --> 00:30:20,390
The groom, Cha Seok Jin.

480
00:30:20,790 --> 00:30:22,460
The bride, Kang Hae Ra.

481
00:30:36,770 --> 00:30:37,770
Congratulations.

482
00:30:37,970 --> 00:30:41,140
May your future together
always be filled with joy.

483
00:30:41,640 --> 00:30:43,780
Please give them another
big round of applause.

484
00:30:46,550 --> 00:30:47,620
My daughter...

485
00:30:49,350 --> 00:30:51,250
You are a beauty.

486
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:52,750
(A Trap Called Desire)

487
00:31:52,820 --> 00:31:55,020
I've checked off
a major requirement in my life.

488
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:57,450
Was Chief Cha a major requirement?

489
00:31:57,520 --> 00:31:59,660
Just head
wherever your heart takes you.

490
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:01,820
There's no need to set
a specific destination.

491
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:04,490
If you head out on this trip,
who'll look after So Yeon?

492
00:32:04,560 --> 00:32:06,730
Why don't you drop by her place,
Director Joo?

493
00:32:06,830 --> 00:32:08,530
Everything's taken care of, right?

494
00:32:08,670 --> 00:32:11,200
Did something happen
between you and Director Joo?

495
00:32:11,270 --> 00:32:13,240
You two seemed quite close.

496
00:32:13,240 --> 00:32:15,970
Give someone an inch,
and she thinks she's all that.

497
00:32:16,040 --> 00:32:18,040
From now on,
you just take what comes.

498
00:32:18,110 --> 00:32:20,240
I'll handle everything for you.

499
00:32:20,380 --> 00:32:22,150
You crazy bum,
who are you trying to scam?

500
00:32:22,210 --> 00:32:25,010
Isn't this proof enough?
Hae Ra, I'm your dad.

501
00:32:25,620 --> 00:32:27,620
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
